WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.470 line:0%
Dan:
<i> We're here to film</i>

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:07.140 line:0%
<i> the Kukkiwon Taekwondo
 Demonstration Team.</i>

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.776 align:start position:0% line:0%
The amount of height
they can get, it is nuts.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:13.446
<i> It's like he's going up
 two flights of stairs
 in two steps.</i>

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:15.314
Dan:
<i> You see the powder
 from the wood.</i>

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:19.719
<i> It's a double spin. Oh!</i>

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.487
 Gav:<i> Just walking
 through the air.</i>

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.223 align:start size:81% position:19%
-<i> That is madness. </i>
- Dan:<i> What?</i>

00:00:24.256 --> 00:00:26.192 align:start position:0%
Oh, man.

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:33.332 align:start position:0% line:0%
Well, I feel
incredibly inadequate.

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:34.801 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
- I know, right?
- I can't do any of that.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.536 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
Just huge impressive
jumps everywhere.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start position:0%
Some of those jumps,
sort of springing off
each other,

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:42.475 size:84% position:42%
I think went higher than
I've ever been on a ladder.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start position:0%
Bloody impressive.
Even some of the intros

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.153 align:start position:0%
and sort of
interstitial moments were
really impressive to watch.

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:55.789 align:start size:75% position:25%
Yeah, their, like,
show introduction piece.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.270
( shouting )

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:12.538 align:start position:0%
I thought it
was so good watching it

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start position:0%
that we actually filmed it
in slo-mo as well.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.794 align:start position:0%
They're so incredibly in sync
the entire time.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.562 align:start size:69% position:31%
Yeah, to find out more
about taekwondo

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:38.564 align:start size:66% position:34%
and the history
of the Kukkiwon team,

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.267 align:start size:69% position:31%
we had a few questions
for their head coach.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.236 line:0%
We're here with Master Park,

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.404 line:0%
who is the head coach
of the Kukkiwon team.

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:47.240 line:0%
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.642 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Thanks very much.
So, um, do people ever

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:50.743 align:start size:66% position:34%
get hit in
the face accidentally

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:51.744 align:start size:63% position:38%
when they're
holding the boards?

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:69% position:31% line:0%
( speaking Korean )

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:59.385 line:0%
A lot.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:02.522 align:start size:59% position:41%
( speaking Korean )

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.258
Kim:<i> As you saw,
 kicks are really strong.</i>

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:10.596
<i> So sometimes if a kicker
 hits a holder's hand,</i>

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.266
<i> sometimes the holder's
 hand is broken.</i>

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.902
<i> Or because when
 the board is broken,</i>

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.904
<i> there's all this debris,
 like, everywhere--</i>

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.340 align:start size:78% position:22%
so sometimes it can cause
deep cuts on your skin.

00:02:21.373 --> 00:02:22.808 align:start size:75% position:25%
I'm glad I wasn't
holding one of those,

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:81% position:19%
because I was thinking
I could probably try that.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.444 align:start size:75% position:25%
But then I saw
the first demonstration.

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:28.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I was like, "Nope!"
- ( shouting )

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:32.585 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Whoa.
- ( shouting )

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:33.920 align:start position:0%
Approximately
how long does it take

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start position:0%
to get good enough
to be on this team?

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.225 align:start size:59% position:41%
( speaking Korean )

00:02:39.258 --> 00:02:41.460
Kim:<i> Most of the members
 start their training</i>

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:43.296
<i> when they are
 in elementary school.</i>

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.631
<i> It requires about seven
 to eight years</i>

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:47.633
<i> of training
 to join the team.</i>

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:50.770 align:start size:78% position:22%
And we select who will be
the demonstrators

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.639 align:start position:0%
- through an annual audition.
- Seven to eight years just to--

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:55.808 align:start size:59% position:41%
And that's just
to be good enough
to get on the team.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.610 align:start size:63% position:38%
And then
you have to audition

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.312 align:start size:84% position:16%
- to be able to
  perform on the team.
- Blimey.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.514 align:start size:75% position:25%
So how long does it take
to become a black belt?

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:04.317 align:start size:59% position:41%
( speaking Korean )

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.719
Kim: So to get
a black belt initially,

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:09.488
<i> it requires about one
 to two years of training.</i>

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:11.324
<i> But to join the team,
 you need to train</i>

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.660
<i> for at least 15 years,
 because after 15 years</i>

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:16.729
<i> you can get
 the fifth-rank black belt.</i>

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:20.233 align:start size:78% position:22%
So you need
the fifth-rank black belt
to even be on the team?

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.867 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Yes.
- 15 years.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.337 align:start size:91% position:9%
Seriously?
So, you can get a black belt,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.339 align:start size:75% position:25%
which I always
thought was like,
"Oh, he's a black belt,"

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.374 align:start size:63% position:38%
in, like, two years,
like it's nothing.

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:31.344 align:start size:66% position:34%
Then 15 years later,
you might get a shot
at being on the team.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.979 align:start position:0%
"I just got my black belt."
Child's play.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.580 align:start size:66% position:34%
Yeah, good luck, pal.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:37.283 align:start position:0%
Wow. Does it hurt
to kick the boards?

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:40.653 align:start size:84% position:16%
- ( speaking Korean )
- Yes.

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:43.856
<i> During your training,
you get to have a thicker skin,</i>

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:46.692
<i> so it gets less painful
 over time.</i>

00:03:46.725 --> 00:03:49.595
<i> It's still painful, but again,
 through your training,</i>

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:53.432
<i>you know how to absorb the heat
 and endure the pain.</i>

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start position:0%
So how many hours per week
do you train?

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.970 align:start size:59% position:41%
( speaking Korean )

00:03:58.003 --> 00:03:59.872
Kim:
<i> So, our Kukkiwon team</i>

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:02.541
<i> usually trains
 about 10 hours a day--</i>

00:04:02.574 --> 00:04:04.010
<i> six hours
 of physical training</i>

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.879
<i> and four hours
 of creating new moves.</i>

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:09.849 align:start size:69% position:31%
You mentioned before
about how people start
in elementary school.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.551 align:start size:63% position:38%
Could I have started
in elementary school
and be this good?

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:16.889 align:start size:75% position:25%
Or does it require
certain physical aspects
and mental strengths?

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.457 align:start size:59% position:41%
( speaking Korean )

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.726
Kim:<i> Starting early
 is not enough.</i>

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.729
<i> At some point you have to get
 professional training.</i>

00:04:23.762 --> 00:04:26.565
<i> But at the same time,
 you need mental skills</i>

00:04:26.598 --> 00:04:30.736
<i> such as endurance, patience,
 and challenging yourself.</i>

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:32.571
<i> So if you are patient enough,</i>

00:04:32.604 --> 00:04:35.908
I guess you could be
as good as our demonstrators.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:39.712 align:start size:75% position:25%
- No discipline.
- No chance.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:41.580 align:start size:53% position:47%
So, what makes
the Kukkiwon team
so special?

00:04:41.613 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:59% position:41%
( speaking Korean )

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.586
Kim:<i> What makes it special
 is two reasons.</i>

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:51.424
<i> First is we are
 the first demonstration team
 that was established,</i>

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.592
<i> and we've set up this system.</i>

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:56.595
<i> There are many demonstration
 teams in Korea,</i>

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:59.065
<i> but the way that the team
 is recognized</i>

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.901
<i>or what kind of moves should be
 included in our performance,</i>

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.770
<i> all this are things
 that we first started.</i>

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:06.939
<i> Then the other reason
 that we're so special</i>

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:10.543
is that we are
a government-funded agency.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:14.447
<i> We travel to
 20 countries across
 the world every year</i>

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.783
<i> to perform and to promote
 taekwondo and Korea.</i>

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:20.853
Dan:<i> Wow. That's a full-on
 professional OG team.</i>

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:23.356 align:start position:0%
Yeah, and for the good
of the industry as well.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.523 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah, exactly.
- Love it.

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:26.092 align:start size:88% position:13%
Thanks very much,
Master Park,

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.462 align:start size:88% position:13%
for shattering
my dreams of becoming
a taekwondo performer.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.463 align:start position:0%
It's just not going to
happen for you.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.897
Not going to happen, is it?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.966 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, that was good.
Back to you, Gav and Dan.

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.001 align:start position:0%
Thanks, us.
That was very interesting.

00:05:36.034 --> 00:05:38.404 align:start position:0%
It's very interesting
doing an interview
with a translator,

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:40.973 align:start size:97% position:3%
- and how quickly
  she could relay information.
- It's very impressive.

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:42.875 align:start position:0%
I was very impressed
by that alone.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:44.410 align:start size:84% position:16%
He said how hard it was
and how much time it takes.

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah.
- I wanted to give it a go.

00:05:46.678 --> 00:05:48.981
But, really,
I just wanted to do
a training montage.

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:50.383
I could tell.
You didn't actually want

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.584
to accomplish anything
long term.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.119
Don't want to learn
any skills.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.653
- Just wanted the montage.
- Just wanted the montage.

00:05:54.686 --> 00:05:56.622 align:start position:0%
Dan, do you want
to show me your montage?

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:57.990 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yes, I do.
- Okay, go on then.

00:05:58.023 --> 00:06:02.528 line:0%
<i> ( synth music playing )</i>

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:09.835
( panting )

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:10.870 align:start position:0%
( shouts )

00:06:12.704 --> 00:06:13.706 align:start position:0%
( muttering )

00:06:17.776 --> 00:06:19.412 align:start position:0%
( shouts )

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:26.686 align:start size:66% position:34%
Oh, wait. I told them
not to put that in!

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.059 align:start size:88% position:13%
( shouts )

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.533
<i> ( ding )</i>

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.801 align:start size:41% position:59%
Don't cringe.

00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:47.907
<i> ( cheers and applause )</i>

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.444 align:start position:0%
Wow. Good montage, Dan.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.112 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Learned some skills.
- Very inspiring.

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:55.047 align:start position:0%
Why don't we put
those skills to use?

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.482 align:start position:0%
I've got some boards
that we can break.

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:57.883
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:06:57.916 --> 00:06:59.485 align:start size:56% position:44%
Already done this,
so, no worries.

00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:01.554 align:start position:0%
You're a professional at this,
so I'll give it a go.

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:04.123 align:start position:0%
Why don't you hold out
this board,

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:05.858 size:81% position:41%
and I'll punch through it.

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:08.694
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.896 align:start position:0%
You sure?
You got to give it
a bit of power.

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:12.064 align:start size:69% position:31%
Yeah, just
a little bit of power?

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:13.199
- Yeah, yeah.
- Just like--

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.500 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah, that's good.
- Yeah.

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:15.835 align:start position:0%
Obviously,
it's quite easy to...

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:16.836 align:start size:53% position:47%
Simple.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:17.903 align:start position:0%
...to break.

00:07:17.936 --> 00:07:18.971 align:start size:50% position:50%
I'll just take
that off of you.

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:21.841 align:start size:88% position:13%
- All right, your turn.
- Okay.

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:23.943 align:start size:31% position:69%
All right.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.078 align:start size:69% position:31%
- Yep.
- You ready?

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:27.547 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Whenever you're ready.
- Okay.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.749
- Aah!
- Ooh.

00:07:30.782 --> 00:07:33.019 align:start position:0%
Didn't quite
get through there.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:50.636 align:start size:88% position:13%
Give me that board.
That's never going to break.

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:54.607 align:start position:0%
Well, what happened was
I bought a plank,
but there was only one.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.275 size:84% position:42%
So I had to get a different
kind of plank for yours.

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:59.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
- And-- a little bit harder.
- This one's solid.

00:07:59.878 --> 00:08:02.047
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.115 align:start position:0%
Ooh, nasty punch, that one,
wasn't it?

00:08:03.148 --> 00:08:06.252
Idiot. Thanks for that, yeah.

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.653 align:start position:0%
So, I thought
it would be good next

00:08:07.686 --> 00:08:09.955 align:start position:0%
to test to see
if you could take a kick.

00:08:09.988 --> 00:08:13.659 align:start position:0%
So I challenged you
to find a taekwondo expert
who could kick you.

00:08:13.692 --> 00:08:15.127 align:start size:66% position:34%
I did find an expert.
A local expert.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.829 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yeah.
- Um, Danica?

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.966 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
Lovely to meet you.
This is our taekwondo expert.

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:22.268 align:start position:0% line:0%
Yeah, nice to meet you,
Danica.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:23.802 align:start position:0% line:0%
How long have you
been doing taekwondo?

00:08:23.835 --> 00:08:26.238 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- Um, three years.
- Three years. Ah, cool.

00:08:26.271 --> 00:08:27.806 align:start size:78% position:22%
- How old are you?
- Seven.

00:08:27.839 --> 00:08:29.842 align:start size:63% position:38%
Seven. That's almost
half your life.

00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:31.710 align:start position:0%
How hard do you think
you can kick Dan?

00:08:31.743 --> 00:08:34.046 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Um, pretty hard.
- Pretty hard.

00:08:34.079 --> 00:08:37.283 align:start size:78% position:22%
Pretty hard?
Look, you're not
supposed to kick me hard.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:40.085 align:start position:0%
I haven't seen her
in action yet,
but I've heard--

00:08:40.118 --> 00:08:41.220 align:start position:0%
I've heard
she can kick hard.

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:43.188 align:start size:59% position:41%
( laughing )
Wha-- oh, man.

00:08:43.221 --> 00:08:44.990 align:start position:0%
So, why don't we put on
some padding?

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:48.160 align:start size:53% position:47%
I've got this
PSI-measuring pad

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:50.029 align:start size:78% position:22%
to be able to test
how hard you can kick me.

00:08:50.062 --> 00:08:51.931 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Put you on.
- I notice you've got
  a red belt on.

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.165 align:start size:63% position:38%
What does that mean?

00:08:53.198 --> 00:08:56.669
It means
I've been in nine belts,

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:59.972
and I'm two belts away
from being a black belt.

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:03.309
- Gav: At age seven.
- That's ridiculous.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:04.843 align:start position:0%
I bet now
you're pretty scared.

00:09:04.876 --> 00:09:06.312 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Can you tie me up?
- Yes.

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:07.846 align:start size:75% position:25%
If I come down here,
you can help me.

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:09.682 size:78% position:61%
You're two belts away
from being a black belt

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:10.683 align:start size:50% position:50%
and you're only
seven years old.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:11.984 align:start size:81% position:19%
That's quite intimidating.

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:13.852 align:start size:91% position:9%
- I bet now you're scared.
- I am now.

00:09:13.885 --> 00:09:15.321 align:start position:0%
I bet now you regret
your decision.

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:17.022 align:start size:63% position:38%
A little bit.
Must be pretty good.

00:09:17.055 --> 00:09:20.225 align:start position:0%
How does this belt
and shoe system work?

00:09:20.258 --> 00:09:24.930 align:start size:66% position:34%
The magnets
connect to the screen

00:09:24.963 --> 00:09:27.199 align:start size:47% position:53%
where the kicks
count them.

00:09:27.232 --> 00:09:28.601 align:start position:0%
So we can see
how hard you kick him.

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:30.869 align:start size:69% position:31%
- All right.
- Okay.

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:32.204 align:start position:0%
Where do you need
Dan to stand for this?

00:09:32.237 --> 00:09:36.208 align:start size:88% position:13%
If I stand here,
you stand just there.

